The goal:
As a store owner, I should be able to manage everything from the admin panel without touching code.

Implement a full content and product management system.

Include:

PRODUCT MANAGEMENT

Admin can create and edit products:

Basic information:

Product name

Short description

Full description

Category

Subcategory

Brand

SKU

Tags

Pricing:

Regular price

Sale price

Discount percentage

Sale start date

Sale end date

Inventory:

Stock quantity

Low stock threshold

Out of stock status

Images:

Upload multiple product images

Change main image

Delete images

Reorder images

PRODUCT VARIATIONS

Support products with options:

Colors:

Add colors

Edit colors

Remove colors

Sizes:

Add sizes

Edit sizes

Remove sizes

Each variation should support:

Separate stock quantity

Separate SKU

Separate price if needed

Separate image if needed

Examples:
A shirt:
Colors:

Black

White

Pink

Sizes:

S

M

L

XL

PROMOTIONS MANAGEMENT

Admin can create promotions:

Discount percentage

Fixed amount discount

Sale products

Category discounts

Coupon codes

Limited time offers

Admin can control:

Start date

End date

Active/inactive

HOMEPAGE CONTENT MANAGEMENT

Admin can update:

Hero banners

Images

Texts

Featured products

Recommended products

Categories shown on homepage

CATEGORY MANAGEMENT

Admin can:

Create categories

Edit categories

Upload category images

Change order

Hide/show categories

CUSTOMER MANAGEMENT

Admin can view:

Customers

Orders history

Total purchases

Notes

Customer status

STORE SETTINGS

Admin can manage:

Store logo

Colors/theme

Contact details

Shipping settings

Payment settings

Social links

ADMIN UX

Create a clear management interface:

Left/right navigation:

Dashboard

Products

Categories

Orders

Customers

Promotions

Homepage

Settings

Make it simple enough for a non-technical store owner.

